-- An @desc or @export written inside a rule written as clauses, where nothing
-- of the rule claims it, is not the next rule's. The bodies of the clauses are
-- not read for annotations, and the rule after took every one written before
-- it, so that an @export between a group's GIVETH and its first clause, or
-- above a definition in the WHERE of one of its clauses, published the rule
-- after the group under that description (refutation of
-- legalese/l4-ide#545's review, round 4). Neither publishes anything here.

-- An @export between the GIVETH and the first clause.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
@export between the GIVETH and the first clause
DECIDE one 0 IS 1
DECIDE one other IS 2

-- An @export above a definition in the WHERE of a clause.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE two 0 IS helper 1
  WHERE
    @export above the helper
    helper x MEANS x + 1
DECIDE two other IS 2

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE three n IS n + 3

#EVAL one 0
#EVAL two 1
#EVAL three 2
